Round-bound hypothesis (coordinator): refuted by reading.

I proposed that rc03_seed56's only-integrated-std::opt red might be the fixed point
stopping at its round bound, so that pruneBranch:817 was running on a graph that
needed one more fold round. The merge lane measured it on this tree's binary:
no pass -> exit 0, no output; std::opt::fold alone -> exit 0, no output;
std::opt -> RuntimeDiag::PassInternalError with three order edges entering
region 5 (28 -> 10, 31 -> 10, 32 -> 10), and no OptimizationStoppedShort.

So the round bound never stopped this program: the optimizer was not short of a
round, it wrote an order edge into a nested region. The original judgement on
pruneBranch:817 stands; "needs a second round of fold" is retired. rounds_warning
(05e331ca3) is unrelated to this red.

